  <section id="faq">
    <h2>What else do people ask about AI ROI?</h2>

    <h3>What is the AI ROI formula?</h3>
    <p>Return on investment is value gained minus total cost, divided by total cost, over the same
       period. For AI, the value is usually the hours saved, priced at what that role costs you. The
       total cost must include setup, training, data clean-up, review and running both ways at once.</p>

    <h3>Is AI worth it for my business?</h3>
    <p>It is worth it where a task is frequent, repetitive and reads or writes things that vary, and
       where the saved time turns into something you can count. It is often not worth it for rare
       tasks or expert judgement where a mistake is costly. The only way to know is to time the work
       first.</p>

    <h3>What is a good AI payback period?</h3>
    <p>There is no honest single number, so be wary of anyone who quotes one before seeing your work.
       A useful test is whether the tool pays back well within the time you expect the process to
       stay the same. If it pays back after your next system change, it never really pays back.</p>

